{"reference":"Isaiah 6","book":"Isaiah","chapter":6,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"historical_context","title":"Holiness, Worship, and Justice","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The vision’s proclamation of YHWH’s holiness and Isaiah’s response in the temple belong to a wider emphasis in Isaiah: YHWH’s holiness is joined to justice and righteousness, and worship is rejected when it coexists with bloodshed, exploitation, or refusal to repair communal wrong.","verse_refs":["Isaiah 6:1-7"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_006_f8aa9f34cbc1ea12d6c2cf86"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"fact"}]},{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Following the Speakers","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Isaiah uses several kinds of speech and narration, including first-person reports, divine speech, royal narratives, communal voices, and personified figures. Speaker identity therefore needs to be established passage by passage. In this chapter, the first-person account of the vision gives way to the Lord’s speech and then to Isaiah’s commissioned message.","verse_refs":["Isaiah 6:1-13"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_006_d1ccb4558f55f9b05066dcb5"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"A Manuscript Witness to Isaiah","blocks":[{"id":"block_3","text":"The Great Isaiah Scroll is an almost complete witness to all sixty-six chapters of Isaiah. It broadly aligns with the Masoretic tradition while also containing many spelling and substantive differences; other Qumran Isaiah manuscripts and interpretive writings show that the book was actively transmitted and interpreted.","provenance_refs":["reader_path_isaiah_006_39f6fe9c04faa9226b952c10"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}